WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.033
-I'm hanging out with the one
and only Fred Armisen! Fred.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:05.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:07.501
Last time, I asked you --

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:10.567
I begged you to do
some impressions, and you did.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:11.834
And you were very nice.

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:15.133
And now I'm asking you again
to do another thing.

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:16.801
I don't know why I'm asking
you to work.

00:00:16.801 --> 00:00:18.400
-Here's what we're gonna do.
-Okay.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.834
-This is something
I'd like to try.

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:21.133
-Alright. This is what
I'm talking about.

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:24.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:26.634
-So, what I want to do is

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:34.234
I want to give examples of
strumming styles.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:38.934
But this is going to be, like,
strumming styles of punk

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:44.067
and alternative music
from 1970 to 2000.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:46.734
This is a sort of
truncated version of, like,

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:49.501
how people played the guitar.

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:51.667
So we'll start with 1970,

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:55.167
and there were fewer, like,
solos and stuff like that.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:56.467
It was a little more rh--

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.267
They had more, like, rhythm
to it and percussion.

00:00:58.267 --> 00:01:04.634
So like, something like Velvet
Underground was kind of like...

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:07.834
♪ Going down the boulevard
with the flower ♪

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:11.467
That kind of thing, right?

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:14.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:15.801
-Boulevard.

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:19.167
-So then like --
So then like mid-'70s,

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:23.033
there was stuff like the Ramones
and stuff at CBGB's,

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:27.968
very driving like...

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:30.467
♪ I just want to watch TV ♪

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:33.367
♪ My baby's giving me
a lobotomy ♪

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:37.601
[ Both singing gibberish ]

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:39.334
That kind of thing.
-Yeah.

00:01:39.334 --> 00:01:42.467
-But then in ---

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:44.667
-Going down the boulevard
with a flower.

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:46.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:51.300
-And then in England, like 1977,
same kind of thing,

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:56.434
but, like, a little more angular
and sort of like...

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.934
♪ Don't go to the ambulance ♪

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:03.300
♪ Don't go to the ambulance,
don't go to the ambulance ♪

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.267
♪ -Don't run on ♪
Yeah, love that.

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.133
-Yeah, that kind of thing.
-Yeah.

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:09.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:13.501
Then like 1980, like post-punk,

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:15.667
they sort of, like, didn't do
chords that much.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:19.801
It was a little bit more like...

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:22.334
♪ I am a neon light ♪

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:26.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:28.767
-Wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:32.133
♪ I am a neon light ♪

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:34.567
♪ I am the neon light ♪

00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:36.400
Yeah, that's great. Love that.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.701
-Then early '80s, there was like

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:41.167
a sort of like country music
feel to, like, punk.

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:44.000
It was kind of like...

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:51.167
[ Singing indistinctly ]

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:52.934
Yeah, that kind of thing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:52.934 --> 00:02:58.934
And then there was like
a sort of mid-'80s, late '80s,

00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:02.200
like Sonic Youth would do this
thing where, like, the chords

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.601
would be a little discordant.

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:10.667
So it'd be like...

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:13.601
♪ Candlelight ♪

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:16.067
♪ On a booth ♪

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:17.434
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:20.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
Wow. That's exactly right. Yeah.

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:21.501
I remember that.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:24.167
-And then do you remember
the early '90s,

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:25.734
like a little ska thing
happening?

00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:28.601
And very playful,
kind of like...

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:29.901
-Yep.

00:03:29.901 --> 00:03:32.334
♪ -Your mom and dad were
the best you ever had ♪

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:36.200
[ Both singing gibberish ]

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.467
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:39.968
-That kind of thing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:44.167
And then Seattle,
Pacific Northwest, you know,

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:46.701
they did a lot of octaves,
like...

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:53.100
Kind of like half time, like...

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.200
♪ Yeah ♪

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:57.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.734 --> 00:03:59.634
♪ Yeah ♪
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:01.167
-Yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:06.634
-Then like, Sleater-Kinney would
be, like, more single notes.

00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:09.400
♪ Don't go, sister ♪

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:12.434
♪ Out of control ♪

00:04:12.434 --> 00:04:14.133
-Yeah, that's right. Love that.

00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:17.767
-And then like 2000,
things got very melodic,

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:21.601
a lot of clear chords, you know.

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:25.400
Like crooning, a lot of,
like, happy singing.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.100
You know, like...

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.467
♪ Come out with me again ♪

00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:34.200
♪ I'd like to take you to
the stratosphere ♪

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.334
Yeah, you know?

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:38.834
[ Both singing indistinctly ]

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:41.133
Kind of like Strokes kind of.
-Yeah, yeah, love that.

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:42.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.534 --> 00:04:47.734
♪♪

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:49.100
Fred Armisen, everybody!

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.267
Season five of "Big Mouth"
premieres Friday on Netflix.

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:54.868
We'll be right back with
a performance from Lucy Dacus.

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:56.501
Stick around, everybody.

00:04:56.501 --> 00:05:01.968
♪♪

